title: IBM TS4300: Power Supplies
agents: snmp
author: Kuhn & Rueß GmbH <info@kuhn-ruess.de>
license: GPL
distribution: none
description:
 Monitors both power supply slots of every chassis of an IBM TS4300 tape
 library. The data comes from the IBM Automation Query MIB
 (chassis-PS1Status / chassis-PS2Status, .1.3.6.1.4.1.2.6.257.1.3.2.1.3
 and .4), which the SNIA-SML-MIB does not cover.

 A power supply reported as {ok} is OK, {not ok} is CRIT. A slot that
 turns {not installed} after discovery is WARN, because the redundancy
 the library was discovered with is gone.

 The serial number of the chassis is shown in the service details.

item:
 Chassis index and power supply number, separated by a slash, for
 example {1/2} for the second power supply of the first chassis.

inventory:
 One service per power supply slot that is populated at discovery time.
